{"total": 48, "offset": 0, "next": 6, "data": [{"paperId": "8ae745da009404a985d1221d2aa39ab80ba849dc", "externalIds": {"ArXiv": "2411.02513", "DOI": "10.4153/S000843952510132X", "CorpusId": 273821210}, "title": "A short proof of the Hilton\u2013Milner Theorem", "venue": "Canadian mathematical bulletin", "year": 2024, "openAccessPdf": {"url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/services/aop-cambridge-core/content/view/F786714A3CDBFE314AABEE4944CD7EEF/S000843952510132Xa.pdf/div-class-title-a-short-proof-of-the-hilton-milner-theorem-div.pdf", "status": "HYBRID", "license": "CCBYSA", "disclaimer": "Notice: Paper or abstract available at https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.02513, which is subject to the license by the author or copyright owner provided with this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."}, "authors": [{"authorId": "2004147078", "name": "Denys Bulavka"}, {"authorId": "2135883", "name": "Russ Woodroofe"}], "abstract": "Abstract We give a short and relatively elementary proof of the Hilton\u2013Milner Theorem."}, {"paperId": "b175faf49b4d4f058183ed19741a0dab599e17f0", "externalIds": {"CorpusId": 261279627}, "title": "Short Proofs of the Kneser-Lov\u00e1sz Coloring Principle 1", "venue": "", "year": 2017, "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null, "disclaimer": "Notice: The following paper fields have been elided by the publisher: {'abstract'}. Paper or abstract available at http://www.math.ucsd.edu/~sbuss/ResearchWeb/KneserLovasz/paper.pdf, which is subject to the license by the author or copyright owner provided with this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."}, "authors": [{"authorId": "2561230185", "name": "James Aisenberg"}, {"authorId": "1974777", "name": "M. Bonet"}, {"authorId": "1764580", "name": "S. Buss"}, {"authorId": "50300780", "name": "Adrian Cr\u01ceciun"}, {"authorId": "1795049", "name": "Gabriel Istrate"}], "abstract": null}, {"paperId": "73c4382747766f5f4b3af35a809a27bf7ea6bac7", "externalIds": {"CorpusId": 261279626}, "title": "Short proofs of the coloring principle", "venue": "", "year": 2017, "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null, "disclaimer": "Notice: The following paper fields have been elided by the publisher: {'abstract'}. Paper or abstract available at https://web.archive.org/web/20210427082944/https://escholarship.org/content/qt0fp705h6/qt0fp705h6.pdf?t=q9pf5k, which is subject to the license by the author or copyright owner provided with this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."}, "authors": [{"authorId": "2561230185", "name": "James Aisenberg"}, {"authorId": "1974777", "name": "M. Bonet"}, {"authorId": "50300780", "name": "Adrian Cr\u01ceciun"}], "abstract": null}, {"paperId": "ad6b6aa4da63a6838b83e8478586a4d13c09bd11", "externalIds": {"MAG": "2963037949", "ArXiv": "1608.06114", "DOI": "10.7494/OPMATH.2017.37.4.597", "CorpusId": 55674958}, "title": "A hierarchy of maximal intersecting triple systems", "venue": "", "year": 2016, "openAccessPdf": {"url": "https://doi.org/10.7494/opmath.2017.37.4.597", "status": "GOLD", "license": "CCBY", "disclaimer": "Notice: Paper or abstract available at https://arxiv.org/abs/1608.06114, which is subject to the license by the author or copyright owner provided with this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."}, "authors": [{"authorId": "2442372", "name": "J. Polcyn"}, {"authorId": "3346977", "name": "A. Ruci\u0144ski"}], "abstract": "We reach beyond the celebrated theorems of Erd\u0151s-Ko-Rado and Hilton-Milner, and, a recent theorem of Han-Kohayakawa, and determine all maximal intersecting triples systems. It turns out that for each $n\\ge7$ there are exactly 15 pairwise non-isomorphic such systems (and 13 for $n=6$). We present our result in terms of a hierarchy of Turan numbers $\\ex^{(s)}(n, M_2^{3})$, $s\\ge1$, where $M_2^{3}$ is a pair of disjoint triples. Moreover, owing to our unified approach, we provide short proofs of the above mentioned results (for triple systems only). The triangle $C_3$ is defined as $C_3=\\{\\{x_1,y_3,x_2\\},\\{x_1,y_2,x_3\\}, \\{x_2,y_1,x_3\\}\\}$. Along the way we show that the largest intersecting triple system $H$ on $n\\ge6$ vertices, which is not a star and is triangle-free, consists of $\\max\\{10,n\\}$ triples. This facilitates our main proof's philosophy which is to assume that $H$ contains a copy of the triangle and analyze how the remaining edges of $H$ intersect that copy."}, {"paperId": "38c1c8d2fd8f39b3d0f8dcf914a2de323948bc5a", "externalIds": {"MAG": "2047848310", "DBLP": "journals/jct/FranklF86", "DOI": "10.1016/0097-3165(86)90121-4", "CorpusId": 39946388}, "title": "Non-trivial intersecting families", "venue": "Journal of Combinatorial Theory", "year": 1986, "openAccessPdf": {"url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/0097-3165(86)90121-4", "status": "BRONZE", "license": null, "disclaimer": "Notice: The following paper fields have been elided by the publisher: {'abstract'}. Paper or abstract available at https://api.unpaywall.org/v2/10.1016/0097-3165(86)90121-4?email=<INSERT_YOUR_EMAIL> or https://doi.org/10.1016/0097-3165(86)90121-4, which is subject to the license by the author or copyright owner provided with this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."}, "authors": [{"authorId": "1678770", "name": "P. Frankl"}, {"authorId": "1733276", "name": "Z. F\u00fcredi"}], "abstract": null}, {"paperId": "08e6a1b9b380a48e15b3739a18bb1f1608cf4860", "externalIds": {"ArXiv": "2206.13485", "CorpusId": 250073181}, "title": "Short injective proofs of the Erd\\H{o}s-Ko-Rado and Hilton-Milner Theorem: A canonical partition of shifted intersecting set systems", "venue": "", "year": 2022, "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null, "disclaimer": "Notice: Paper or abstract available at https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.13485, which is subject to the license by the author or copyright owner provided with this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."}, "authors": [{"authorId": "2470902750", "name": "T. Nguy\u1ec5n"}, {"authorId": "2493240383", "name": "Thi-Quynh-Trang Nguyen"}], "abstract": "A BSTRACT . We give a canonical partition of shifted intersecting set systems, from which one can obtain uni\ufb01ed and elementary proofs of the Erd\u02ddos-Ko-Rado and Hilton-Milner Theorem, as well as a characterization of maximal shifted k -uniform intersecting set systems over [ n ] ."}]}
